{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>I am gathered to my people.</b> Because they bring the souls into their place of storage — for אֲסִיפָה in the Hebrew language is a term of bringing in, as in ״וְאֵין אִישׁ מְאַסֵּף אוֹתִי הַבַּיְתָה״ (Judges 19), ״וַאֲסַפְתּוֹ אֶל תּוֹךְ בֵּיתֶךָ״ (Deuteronomy 22), ״בְּאָסְפְּכֶם אֶת תְּבוּאַת הָאָרֶץ״ (Leviticus 23) — bringing them into the house because of the rains; ״בְּאָסְפְּךָ אֶת מַעֲשֶׂיךָ״ (Exodus 23) — and every אֲסִיפָה mentioned in connection with death is likewise a term of bringing in." "<b>Unto my fathers.</b> With my fathers."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:20.462357845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}